    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_024                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D3                          
                                                                              
    Post-Flight Load and Penetration Calibration Table                        
                                                                              
    This handwritten table gives the post-flight load and penetration         
    calibration data for the Apollo 15 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer      
    (LSRP) flight unit S/N 2003, lunar drum S/N 2002. The tests were done on  
    11-12 August 1971 at the Manned Space Center in Houston.  The notes       
    indicate the calibration was done "using the bottom half of unit S/N      
    2002 - Deadweight loading on jig". The upper part of the table gives the  
    load calibration. The first column gives the index number corresponding   
    to the initial stting on the LSRP.  The second column, "vert. scribe",    
    gives the initial angle  (degrees, minutes, seconds) read on the drum.    
    The following columns are for different loads put on the LSPRP, listed    
    at the top of the column in kilograms and Newtons.  The entries in the    
    columns give the reading on the drumm and the difference between that     
    and the original reading.  The lower part of the table gives the          
    penetration calibration as cathetometer reading in centimeters.  See      
    page D-4, A15_SMSS_71_M016935_025, for further details.                   
                                                                              
